# Our deltas on top of the base, and what each one is.
#
# THE BASE IS WineCX 26.3.0 -- CodeWeavers' published CrossOver Wine source, in
# src/crossover/sources/wine at tag winecx-26.3.0. Not upstream Wine.
#
#   fix        upstreamable; the goal is to send it away and delete it here
#   workaround ours to carry until the base changes
#   debug      diagnostic only; NOT applied by default (build-runtime --with-debug)
#
# A patch here that ports a `CW HACK` is a smell: it means we are re-deriving
# something the base already carries, which is the whole thing the pivot was
# meant to stop. Take it from the base instead. Four patches left for exactly
# that reason -- see patches/superseded/README.md. Earlier dlopen/soname patches
# were wrong rather than superseded -- see patches/retracted/README.md.
#
# class       patch
# MEASURED 2026-07-31, and this is why it is back: the pivot test says CrossOver's
# CX HACK 23950 does NOT replace this. On winecx-26.3.0 with no injection, Steam's
# window is black, the 23950 shm-surface path never fires for CEF windows (zero
# shm_surface traces across 78 wine pids on +win, in a log that does contain
# CefBrowserWindow and Chrome_WidgetWin_0/1), and CrossOver never modified
# winemac.drv/surface.c -- the `/* use default surface */` line that drops
# cross-process blits is byte-identical to upstream. 23950 keys on a foreign
# *parent*; our bug is a foreign *painter*. See docs/RUNTIME.md section 2.
workaround    wine-0004-kernelbase-append-args-env.patch
# CodeWeavers' msync leaked one wait registration every time the client's
# contention shortcut fired: it returned STATUS_PENDING without unregistering,
# so the server kept the thread on the wait list of every unsignaled object.
# On an event that never fires (a worker's quit event) the list only grows,
# until the 0x80000-node pool is exhausted ("msync: warn: node memory pool
# exhausted", all cores busy). Measured with wine-0006 + tools/probes/waitprobe:
# leaked nodes == registrations without unregister == contention returns.
# Candidate to report to CodeWeavers.
fix           wine-0007-msync-unregister-on-contention.patch
debug         wine-0005-winemac-surface-flush-trace.patch
# Fantasy General II, 2026-10-02: after long play, wineserver floods
# "msync: warn: node memory pool exhausted" and all cores saturate. The pool is
# 0x80000 wait registrations, so they are leaking. Counts adds/removes/signal
# frees in wineserver and the client's contention shortcut (which returns
# without unregistering). Silent unless WINEMSYNC_STATS=1.
debug         wine-0006-msync-node-pool-stats.patch

# DXMT (built separately, see backends/)
fix           dxmt-0001-include-iomanip.patch
